  "real_mix": "scripts/qa/nemotron3/channel_score.py: per-10 ms track-energy weak reference (active above -45 dBFS, quiet below -60 dBFS, 200 ms bridging and minimum run), many-to-one side mapping, on the microphone plus system mix",
  "real_system_track": "the product's input (system track); disagreement is strict DER of each system against baseline-cpu",
  "judge": "scripts/qa/nemotron3/judge_pack.py: product ASR segments labelled by each system's system-track turns (largest overlap), 3 windows of 60 segments per meeting (seed 64), systems shown as columns A and B in random order with labels renumbered; one model judge per language class counted plausibly wrong remote lines without the key",
  "segment_assignment": "scripts/qa/nemotron3/score_segments.py (R6): baseline-cpu and nemotron-cpu-int8 label segments with the speaker pass's rule (crates/dettivo-meeting/src/diarize.rs: most-overlap speaker when at least 0.25 of the span is diarized speech and it holds at least 0.6 of that speech, otherwise none); nemotron-cpu-int8+segment uses the adapter. Real meetings: the product's remote (system-track) segments from the Dettivo database. AMI test split, automatic count: segments cut once from the only_words reference turns and once by Whisper; labelled segments become turns scored with diarization_score.py (ADR 0058), and a line view gives each line the reference speaker with the most overlap and counts labelled lines whose label differs under the best one-to-one mapping. Port check: the Python rule on baseline-cpu turns against the labels the product stored for the same meetings.",
  "judge_r6": "a fresh pack from scripts/qa/nemotron3/judge_pack.py --rule product: the same 8 meetings, 3 windows of 60 segments per meeting with seed 65, the three systems as columns A, B and C in random order per window with labels renumbered; one model judge per language class, same counting protocol, without the key. The judges' labelled and unlabelled line counts matched the packets exactly in all 72 columns"
 },
